# Cloudflare Pages reads _headers from the deploy root. Everything in public/
# is copied verbatim into .output/public, which is the directory Pages serves -
# same path robots.txt takes.
#
# The CSP is Report-Only on purpose. Violations show up in the browser console
# (there is no report collector wired up) and block nothing. Read the notes
# under connect-src before switching the header name to Content-Security-Policy.

# The landing loops are large and never change within a deploy, so they are
# cached hard. Deliberately NOT `immutable` and deliberately not a year: these
# filenames are not content-hashed, and the release process re-renders them in
# place, so the same URL can legitimately hold different bytes after a deploy.
# A year of `immutable` on a mutable name would pin a visitor to the old video
# with no way to invalidate it.
#
# No `stale-while-revalidate` either, for the same reason: it let a re-rendered
# loop keep being served from cache for up to a week after the deploy that
# replaced it. A day of plain `max-age` is the whole exposure now.
#
# Give these names a content hash and this becomes `max-age=31536000,
# immutable` - that is the fix, and it is the only thing blocking it.
/landing/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://eu-assets.i.posthog.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; media-src 'self'; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://iteuwqbqrulwdwyjohtx.supabase.co wss://iteuwqbqrulwdwyjohtx.supabase.co https://eu.i.posthog.com https://eu-assets.i.posthog.com https://openrouter.ai; manifest-src 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests
